OSI Model — Detailed

OSI = Open Systems Interconnection

It is a 7-layer reference model used to understand how network communication works.

7  Application
6  Presentation
5  Session
4  Transport
3  Network
2  Data Link
1  Physical

Remember:

All People Seem To Need Data Processing

First understand the big picture

Suppose your browser wants to send:

Hello Google

The application gives the data to the lower layers.

Each layer adds information needed by that layer.

This is called encapsulation.

Application
    │
    │ Data
    ↓
Transport
    │
    │ Segment
    ↓
Network
    │
    │ Packet
    ↓
Data Link
    │
    │ Frame
    ↓
Physical
    │
    │ Bits
    ↓
Network

At the receiver, the opposite happens.

This is called decapsulation.

