Very important: Segmentation vs Fragmentation

You specifically asked about segmentation, so don't confuse these.

Segmentation

Usually associated with Transport layer, especially TCP.

Application data
       ↓
TCP
       ↓
Segment 1
Segment 2
Segment 3

TCP divides its byte stream into segments for transmission.

IP fragmentation

Different concept.

If an IPv4 packet is too large for a link's MTU and fragmentation is permitted, IP may fragment it.

Large IP packet
       ↓
IP fragmentation
       ↓
Fragment 1
Fragment 2
Fragment 3

So:

TCP segmentation ≠ IP fragmentation.

Modern networks generally try to avoid IP fragmentation through mechanisms such as Path MTU Discovery.

