Where does OSI fit?

This is an important distinction.

DNS itself is an application-layer protocol.

So DNS is part of the OSI Layer 7 discussion.

The DNS lookup itself still uses lower layers to transport the DNS query.

For example, a traditional DNS query often uses:

Application → DNS
Transport   → UDP/TCP
Network     → IP
Data Link   → Ethernet/Wi-Fi
Physical    → Signals

Modern DNS can also use other transports such as DNS over TLS or DNS over HTTPS, so the exact transport path can differ.

